   "note_now": "WITHHELD 2026-08-30 by the orchestrator on EXP-0189's eighth cannot-fail finding. This row was promoted through `EXP-0179/analysis/analyze.py:140-142`, whose promotion gate has **no `moved >= 1` conjunct** -- `len(moved)` sits only in the right arm of an `or` whose left arm is `disagreements == 0`, so a perfectly reproducible, perfectly INERT field passes. EXP-0189 proved it constructively rather than by argument: a synthetic DEAD-CODE carrier fed to the unmodified pipeline yields `{\"label\":\"hardware-run\",\"movement\":0,\"range\":\"0..255 dense (all 256 values), 2 carriers\"}` -- **byte-for-byte the string published for this field**. Its sibling `call.b6` rode the same branch and was caught only because an independent second method (arm S, mutating the real compiler-emitted call) refuted it; `call.tail` never got a second method. The measurement may well be right -- inert is a plausible reading -- but it is indistinguishable from dead code under the gate that produced it, and that is not evidence. Needs a second method or a re-run under a gate with the missing conjunct.",
